\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Formal position, career, and interaction counts (person-year). Poisson pseudo-maximum likelihood; standard errors clustered by person in parentheses. The outcome is the number of gifts received in year $t$. Columns 1 and 3 compare people (B), with year and current-sector fixed effects. Columns 2 and 4 compare the same person over time (W), with person and year fixed effects. Career length drops out of the within-person models because it is collinear with person and year fixed effects. Columns 3--4 exclude everyone who ever held a cabinet-level office. * $p<0.05$, ** $p<0.01$, *** $p<0.001$.}}{18}{table.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rev_position}{{7}{18}{Formal position, career, and interaction counts (person-year). Poisson pseudo-maximum likelihood; standard errors clustered by person in parentheses. The outcome is the number of gifts received in year $t$. Columns 1 and 3 compare people (B), with year and current-sector fixed effects. Columns 2 and 4 compare the same person over time (W), with person and year fixed effects. Career length drops out of the within-person models because it is collinear with person and year fixed effects. Columns 3--4 exclude everyone who ever held a cabinet-level office. * $p<0.05$, ** $p<0.01$, *** $p<0.001$}{table.caption.18}{}}
