\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {C3}{\ignorespaces Characteristics shared by the giver and the recipient of each gift, compared with random pairings. The unit is a gift whose giver and recipient both have QIDs. ``Gifts'' counts those for which the characteristic is recorded for both people. The two baselines shuffle givers among gifts reported in the same year, or in the same branch and year, and average 500 permutations. ``Ratio'' is observed over the branch-year baseline. $p$ is the share of branch-year permutations at least as large as the observed value. ``Professional career'' groups occupations into military, diplomat, law, economics/business, academic, and civil servant (``politician'' is excluded). Panel B drops gifts reported by the White House and Congress.}}{41}{table.caption.55}\protected@file@percent }
